"I'll run the script fresh, capture the output to a file, and note any deadlock errors.Done. Ran the script and captured the output to `deadlock_output.txt`.\n\n**Deadlock occurred.** Error message noted:\n\n> `sqlite3.OperationalError: database is locked`\n\n**Sequence of events:**\n\n1. Thread A began and updated account 1, then slept holding its transaction open\n2. Thread B began and updated account 2, then slept holding its transaction open\n3. Both threads then reached for the account the other had locked: circular wait formed\n4. SQLite resolved it by failing Thread B with `database is locked` (SQLITE_BUSY), which the script caught and rolled back\n\n**Outcome:**\n\n| Thread | Result |\n|--------|--------|\n| A | committed (both updates applied) |\n| B | deadlocked, rolled back, no changes applied |\n\nThe script exited with code 0 since it handles the error gracefully. Final balances: account 1 = 106, account 2 = 106 (only Thread A's increments applied)."